# Exam Lines - Environment Configuration Example
#
# No environment variables are required to build or run Exam Lines.
# The project has zero npm dependencies and runs in pure client-side ES Modules.
#
# Commands:
#   npm test       - Runs the test suite via Node's built-in test runner (node --test)
#   npm run build  - Inlines all modules and styles into dist/exam-lines.html and dist/index.html
#
# AI Question Generation:
# - On claude.ai: No API key is needed; the built-in window.claude capability is used.
# - In self-hosted copies: Each viewer connects their own API key (Gemini, Claude, or OpenAI-compatible)
#   directly in the browser via the "AI Settings" dialog. Keys are stored solely in that browser's
#   localStorage and are sent directly to the selected provider endpoint in a request header.
#
# CAUTION:
# Never commit a real API key to source control! The build process inlines all source files
# into public, client-facing HTML files.
